# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/sampler window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/sampler and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image, its stop rule and its minutes. The image is tp4-serve-6 throughout: SB builds it, the
# later jobs serve it, and a commit after SB's tag needs a new tag and every later job the new one.
# SB: build tp4-serve-6 and smoke the PRODUCTION configuration: c2-packed-tp4, the traffic profile, audits ON, the tail caps ON. This
# image adds, all off by default, the two sampler arms (QWEN_FAST_PACKED_SAMPLER_PREWARM, QWEN_FAST_PACKED_SAMPLER_IN_TRACE); the
# production profile sets neither, so this job is tp4-serve-4's production configuration on the new image. A hang or a refusal on it
# stops the window. The test list is tp4-serve-4's B4 list unchanged. READ the log: no UNQUALIFIED line, no late prefill program,
# c2_smoke_check clean with audit_mismatches 0, no watchdog or replay-deadline exit, and no '[PINDIAG] packed sampler arm' line (the
# arms are off here).
# Duration (estimate): 45 min. Stop rule: a hang on this configuration stops the window.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset build smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-6
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady,steady_resend,tool_call,stream_tool_call,stream_reasoning,refused_n2,alive_after_refusal,stream_dropped,alive_after_drop,concurrent4_solo,concurrent4_code,concurrent4_code_equal
